Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Fix undefined column error in exercise handlers by
 removing non-existent DB fields

- Updated `handlers/exercise_params.py` to fetch only existing columns (`id`, `name`, `muscle_group`, etc.) and retrieve 1RM from `user_tests` instead of `exercises.one_rm_kg`.
- Modified `handlers/workouts.py` to remove references to `default_sets`, `default_reps_min`, and `one_rm_kg` in SQL queries, using hardcoded defaults or dynamic 1RM lookup.
- Implemented `_get_user_one_rm` helper to safely fetch the latest test weight for a user-exercise pair.
- Adjusted parameter parsing and finalization logic to handle missing default values gracefully without crashing on database schema mismatches.
